{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age","id":776526,"title":"[2ed] Do Werewolves age?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-29T05:39:30-08:00","id":776526,"title":"[2ed] Do Werewolves age?","content":"Can someone knowledgeable please tell how is it in second edition with werewolves ageing or not?<br /> Has Primal Urge to do anything with it any more (or is it left for interpretation)?<br /> What about the Gift called &quot;Ties of Blood and Bone&quot;, what happens if a venerate pack member targets a young one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9813-blankbadger","name":"blankbadger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:19:27-08:00","id":776541,"title":"","content":"There's next to nothing written on the subject at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T08:22:33-08:00","id":776595,"title":"","content":"Unless specifically stated otherwise, all supernaturals default to the same rules as mortals. So, a werewolf ages like a mortal, regains willpower through rest like a mortal, and needs to eat and drink like a mortal. Some people rule that high PU wolves don't age, but that's not official.<br /> <br /> Ties of Blood and Bone actually is a teleport effect - the two swap places, they don't merge or affect each other physically, save for that healing effect with an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T08:51:45-08:00","id":776609,"title":"","content":"So is the a way for a werewolf to avoid dying of old age? Beside the obvious deus ex machina approach of making up something akin to a &quot;Spirit of Immortal Noodles&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT Influence: Immortality 3 Noodles 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9813-blankbadger","user":"blankbadger","date":". 11-29-2015, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9813-blankbadger","name":"blankbadger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:09:56-08:00","id":776621,"title":"","content":"Re: Werewolf Aging<br /> <br /> While it is a first edition source, <i><b>Blood of the Wolf</b></i> (pg.31-32) goes into a good amount of detail into Werewolf physiology. As far a aging is concerned, Werewolf regeneration extends the lifespan and slows the aging process, with the oldest known Werewolves reaching the 110's with no real drop off in health and ability until around 80. The same section suggests that Primal Urge retards aging even further, with the highest levels turning the Werewolf into an ageless God Monster. As noted, there has been no official word on how much this still applies in 2nd Edition, it wouldn't be unreasonable to treat it as canon until officially updated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T10:25:45-08:00","id":776670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blankbadger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=776609#post776609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is the a way for a werewolf to avoid dying of old age? Beside the obvious deus ex machina approach of making up something akin to a &quot;Spirit of Immortal Noodles&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of Werewolf's first offerings Olivia Citysmith, arguably the alpha of alphas of Chicago, made a deal with Lamashtu, one of the Maeljin, for 'unending youth and vigor.' So these things aren't exactly unheard of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:33:42-08:00","id":776696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=776621#post776621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Werewolf Aging<br /> <br /> While it is a first edition source, <i><b>Blood of the Wolf</b></i> (pg.31-32) goes into a good amount of detail into Werewolf physiology. As far a aging is concerned, Werewolf regeneration extends the lifespan and slows the aging process, with the oldest known Werewolves reaching the 110's with no real drop off in health and ability until around 80. The same section suggests that Primal Urge retards aging even further, with the highest levels turning the Werewolf into an ageless God Monster. As noted, there has been no official word on how much this still applies in 2nd Edition, it wouldn't be unreasonable to treat it as canon until officially updated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have to deal with menopause - no thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9813-blankbadger","name":"blankbadger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:43:13-08:00","id":776702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blankbadger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=776696#post776696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You still have to deal with menopause - no thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally ignore that part. Wolves don't go through menopause or it's male equivalent , so why should werewolves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:05:41-08:00","id":776717,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, spirits are immortals, so why shouldn't werewolves be? Which is, for the most part, the reasoning for why really powerful werewolves would become ageless.<br /> <br /> Still, very powerful and old werewolves are likely to be rare, as they only get that way by hunting. And since they're not gaming the system, they're hunting increasingly more powerful things. At a certain point, failure means death. Plus if they all survived you'd have a horde of immortal predators that death rage for 12 hours a time. Which is about a scary a thought as the ancient vampires that control entire countries through their age-entrenched manipulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:17:56-08:00","id":776730,"title":"","content":"I could've sworn one of the settings in the 2e core mentions Primal Urge prolonging life to an absurd degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:31:38-08:00","id":776740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=776730#post776730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could've sworn one of the settings in the 2e core mentions Primal Urge prolonging life to an absurd degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably thinking of Lycaon-Ur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition; The Field of Dogs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not Lycaon-Ur is who he claims to be \u2014 once-King of Arcadia, turned into a werewolf by Zeus \u2014 it is undeniable that he is an ancient and terrifying predator. He is eternally hungry, his maw a conduit to something else, some angelic furnace of raw Essence. If he is a werewolf, then Lycaon\u2019s Primal Urge long since reached such potency that he has begun to turn into something greater. He certainly has the spiritual power to serve as patron for the lodge that has gathered around him.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few other parts of the book that suggest there is something beyond being a werewolf. From the Path of the Storm Lords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secret rites performed within the tribe hint at the idea that the Uratha are more than just the descendants of Father Wolf \u2014 they are his heirs, and a werewolf who faces the crucible of the hunt and emerges stronger for it can raise herself up beyond flesh. They call this process Abni-Gur, the crucible of becoming. They say that a Storm Lord (and it\u2019s always a Storm Lord in the stories) who masters her Harmony and makes herself one with her Primal Urge will one day ascend to take Father Wolf\u2019s place as Lord of the Boundary. </div> </div> </div>To a couple different sections on Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It [Primal Urge] reflects her progress through the Siskur-Dah, following the footsteps of Urfarah to become a bodhisattva predator, a true inheritor of Mother Wolf\u2019s legacy. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As her Primal Urge increases, a werewolf sheds her human upbringing. She becomes closer to the Goddess of the Hunt, the ultimate predator. A few werewolves, those who follow the raging beast within, feel the drive to become something more \u2014 akin to the Firstborn, or even to Father Wolf himself. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T14:11:47-08:00","id":776799,"title":"","content":"There may be multiple outcomes for elder werewolves then.<br /> <br /> It appears from the book that high Primal Urge werewolves could easily fall into the trap of staying in the shadow permanently and most likely end up becoming a spirit. I am not sure if this would be considered unsatisfactory existence.<br /> <br /> A flesh-leaning high PU werewolf looks hard to do. It seems like something that could easily become corrupted by other supernatural forces and would be looked upon in horror. It would need to find a way to get essence without eating wolves, humans, or werewolves or abandoning its pack. A pack of werewolves that exclusively looks for spirits on this side of the gauntlet may be possible but a diet of essence would be hard to satisfy. <br /> <br /> Maintaining harmony and becoming high primal urge would be the real trick and may be the key to unlocking a truly higher state of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T14:34:21-08:00","id":776812,"title":"","content":"I don't think they'd become a spirit, though they'd certainly lean heavily on their spirit side. And a flesh-leaning wolf wouldn't be that hard, the Sacred Hunt is the big way to get Essence and the anchors and touchstones would help.<br /> <br /> The big thing is for werewolves to accept that they aren't human, they aren't spirits, or wolves, they're a thing of their own, Pangaeans. It's hard, because there's not exactly a lot of beings other than fellow werewolves you can run into and expect to appreciate the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T15:04:08-08:00","id":776829,"title":"","content":"Aren't Shartha Pangeans? And they're essentially immortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T15:16:01-08:00","id":776835,"title":"","content":"They seem to be Pangaeans, but they don't have the same situation going for them, and they certainly don't want to bond over their similarities. They've got a weird sort of reincarnation thing going on, as shards are gobbled up by particularly successful shartha, then split again and maybe a shard finds a host again and starts developing a life. All in all they lean more towards the spirit side of things, having the 'spirit' side of the Pangean, but not the flesh, which they have to take from the real world.<br /> <br /> Though yeah on their own they're immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-29-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T22:53:11-08:00","id":777015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=776702#post776702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally ignore that part. Wolves don't go through menopause or it's male equivalent , so why should werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because <i><b>Blood of the Wolf </b></i>says so :/ But this is 2ed we are talking about so nobody knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9813-blankbadger","name":"blankbadger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T00:43:01-08:00","id":777041,"title":"","content":"'... A Hishu Uratha is more human than human, and blends into a crowd.' (WtF2, p96)<br /> <br /> Female Uratha menstruating well beyond the normal human age for menopause would be a very poor disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T00:54:19-08:00","id":777043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=777041#post777041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Female Uratha menstruating well beyond the normal human age for menopause would be a very poor disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the disguise assisted by retarding the visual signs of aging. Your one hundred and seventy year old werewolf crone could look like a fit thirty-something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T01:02:56-08:00","id":777045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=777043#post777043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the disguise assisted by retarding the visual signs of aging. Your one hundred and seventy year old werewolf crone could look like a fit thirty-something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suffice it to be said, though, that it's a lot easier to play off a lack of menstruation during the apparent-age range in which menstruation is an expected concern compared to the inverse.<br /> <br /> The loquacious mute draws more attention than the silent announcer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T01:53:00-08:00","id":777057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=777043#post777043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the disguise assisted by retarding the visual signs of aging. Your one hundred and seventy year old werewolf crone could look like a fit thirty-something.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Blood of the Wolf*, werewolves don't suffer ageing effects until 90-100 years old, and typically look about half their age. As human women (on average) experience menopause around 45-55 years, 90-110 is probably when Uratha would experience menopause.**<br /> <br /> tl;dr IMO, Delayed menopause works, no menopause makes for poor disguise.***<br /> <br /> * AFAIK, nothing has been discussed about what carries over from 1st to 2nd ed.<br /> ** This is academic only, as I can only see a couple of in game scenarios where it would be relevant. <br /> *** If it comes to a discussion, I'd recommend 2nd ed Uratha age at the same rate as the humans around them, as they're meant to be perfectly disguised.**** Besides which, apart from seeding a few ancient NPCs, longevity is almost never a factor in WtF games. <br /> **** Except perhaps at PU 10, when the pure spirit Uratha sheds her fleshy shell and becomes something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T09:43:15-08:00","id":777202,"title":"","content":"I can't even see where aging would have much relevance in current second edition games. I mean I suppose it's possible people are doing time jumps but without rules, or even with first edition rules, you have the standard World of Darkness default on the matter. 'You don't know, maybe it happens, there's certainly stories about it.'<br /> <br /> That said if the aging thing was off by a few years it would explain the first edition pictures of Uratha, most of whom appeared to be in the prime of their life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:42:56-08:00","id":780061,"title":"","content":"In my games I use high PU to make a werewolf ageless. But like everyone says, that sort of scenario doesn't happen very much since werewolves are constantly hunting dangerous foes. Though recently my group and I started playing are own Dark Eras setting, taking place in the Wild West, New Mexico till modern day. We had the same problem about age so we experimented the situation. Of course we use the high PU technique but some of us didn't reach it in time.... So at the end we ended up playing ageless werewolves, which turned out to be pretty fun, if I do say so myself. But hey, that was our game. Do whatever fits your game and makes it fun for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T16:03:52-08:00","id":798008,"title":"","content":"Personally - as in, in the unique environment of my comparatively crossover heavy games specifically - I would not have ageless Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Long lived and healthy certainly. But living forever is rather more of a core conceit for Vampires and Mummies while it is more of an incidental quirk for Werewolves. To become ageless I'd have Werewolves have to find someway of becoming more Spirit, like the Firstborn, more totemic and ascending to a different form rather than being mostly a regular character who happens to have hundreds of XP and PU10 bopping around at 2,312 years of age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T16:19:17-08:00","id":798010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/776526-2ed-do-werewolves-age?p=798008#post798008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">being mostly a regular character who happens to have hundreds of XP and PU10 bopping around at 2,312 years of age.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Primal Urge 10 werewolf can only gain sustenance from Essence, needs to engage in the Sacred Hunt at least once every three days to stave off loss of Essence and Harmony gain, and suffers episodes of Death Rage for twelve hours, which is why the consensus seems to be fine with increasing agelessness at higher Primal Urge \u2014 it doesn't mean much for a character whose requisite lifestyle all but ensures an inevitable Bigger Fish and/or vanishing into the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T16:24:23-08:00","id":798012,"title":"","content":"I think saying &quot;aging is irrelevant to a normal game&quot; does miss something important - it's probably irrelevant to the PCs over the game's timescale unless they have a unique reason to care, but it affects NPC generation.<br /> <br /> If it's reasonable for there to be an ancient werewolf who remembers fighting in World War 1 around and still going strong, STs have access to some Fun and Games that might inspire an interesting setting element or plot thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T00:44:47-08:00","id":798152,"title":"","content":"From a pure mechanics point of view, I\u00b4d say that verewolves do age at a given rate, but their healing factor prevents them from suffering any harmful effects tied to aging so, ancient werewolves would have its hair become grey, others could lose it, skin could look like that of an elder person, but wouldn\u00b4t suffer any loss of muscle mass or bone density, nor any internal organ degradation as those effects are a direct consecuence of a lower cell regen rate that comes with age, something that werewolves doesn\u00b4t seem to suffer, but the opposite even more if they increase PU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T10:08:23-08:00","id":798305,"title":"","content":"An Uratha who lacks prominent amounts of Primal Urge (6+) only begins to see the signs of middle age (40+) at around 90 or 100 (I assume this to be the mild effects, like articulation aches), according to first edition. Past a threshold where their only sustenance is literally spirit stuff (essence, and mind, every Uratha can survive exclusively on the stuff) it comes to mind they benefit from a spirit-like agelessness.<br /> <br /> The flesh is weak, the shadow remembers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T17:42:14-08:00","id":798509,"title":"","content":"It's not really touched upon in the core, but I always hold that werewolves age more slowly at higher Primal Urge, to the point of eventually becoming immortal. Especially at Primal Urge 10, where as Satchel pointed out, you're probably more spirit than flesh, and have long ago left humanity behind. And you know what's cool about it? If someone ever runs a high-powered, high-Experiences game with vampires or mummies or whatever, it lets you play an equally ancient werewolf (perhaps awoken from slumber in the <i>Hisil</i>) and get to be a real monster among monsters. So much flavor to be had there.<br /> <br /> Them: &quot;You just awoke. How long have you been slumbering in that cave?&quot;<br /> You: &quot;The herd still lived in dens of thatch and mud.&quot;<br /> Them: &quot;Holy shit, how are you going to adjust? There's so much that's changed.&quot;<br /> You: &quot;No. One year, ten, a thousand. The hunt remains the same. And I grow hungry. Let me show you how the strongest hunt, pup.&quot;<br /> Them: &quot;What serves as prey to a millennia-old <i>Uratha</i>?&quot;<br /> You: &quot;<i>Everything</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}